      "modelLabel": "Auto Intelligence (Cursor)",
      "permissionMode": "auto-approve",
      "prompt": "Implement this. First plan it out. Then implement. All locally. Make sure to verify it works. Commit everything locally. These are tools we should expose to the agent here in argmax, similar to what we do for other things like the browser etc.\n\n1. **Attention on `session_status` and `session_list`** — one field, already persisted, and it answers the question a launcher actually has: does a person need to look? This absorbs the \"approvals visibility\" item. A separate `approvals_list` is not worth it while auto-approve is the default.\n2. **`checks_run`** — `checks:run` IPC exists. Makes goal evaluation and \"is the child done\" evidence-based instead of prose-based. Unchanged from before.\n3. **`workspace_status` plus bounded `workspace_diff`, taking an optional `session`** — the other list is right that Argmax knows things Bash cannot see: shared versus isolated checkout, tracked PR, archive eligibility. But for the caller's own tree `git status` already works, so the real gap is reading a peer's workspace. Build it session-addressable from the start. The `review:*` handlers cover the diff.\n4. **`learnings_add` then `learnings_search`** — only after a writer exists does the read pay off. This is the one memory path that works for all five providers. Demote the other list's \"memory read\" until this lands.\n5. **`terminal_spawn` / `terminal_read`** — I keep this higher than the other list did. Each follow-up relaunches the CLI, so a dev server started from Bash dies between turns. Argmax's PTY is the only process that survives a turn, and it is user-visible. The \"is something already running here\" read is the same tool.\n6. **`browser_console` / `browser_network`** — the one browser addition that matters for a coding agent checking its own web change. The CDP channel is there.\n7. **`project_list`** — small but real. `session_list` with `all` only reveals projects that have open sessions. `project_info` with check commands and defaults can wait until `checks_run` needs it.\n8. **`schedule_followup`** — wake this session at a time. Replaces `session_wait` polling for CI and deploys. `routines:*` IPC exists.\n9. **`session_launch` extras** — `reasoning` and `permissionMode`. Cheap.",
